Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

All,

In our C900 Product Line there are Tapped Tees/Service Tees.  These tees ha=
ve female threaded outlets and are used for service line connections to mai=
n lines.  These fittings are pressure rated complying with AWWA C907, the p=
roduct standard for molded pressure rated PVC fittings for Cast Iron Outsid=
e Diameter (CIOD) PVC pipe complying with AWWA C900.

There is a difference in form of our 4" C907 Tapped Tee/Service Tee compare=
d to the 6" & 8".

Note the difference in the branches of the three sizes found in the first t=
hree attachments all of which have 2" threaded outlets.  The file names ind=
icate the fitting size.

The 4" branch has a shorter but wider shape.  The diameter of the 4" branch=
 is relatively large and constant regardless of female thread diameter.  In=
 the larger fittings the branches stand off further from the body and the b=
ranch thickness changes with the diameter of the female thread diameter and=
 is thinner than the branch in the 4" fittings.  The branch of the 4" is so=
 short it is more accurately referred to as a "boss".

The reason for this difference is due to the pressure rating method of AWWA=
 C907 (the product standard these fittings must comply with) and the mechan=
ics in play.  There is what is called a scale effect.  The external reinfor=
cement provided by the branch design in the 4" Tapped Tee when tested accor=
ding to the standard passes the standard's criteria for pressure rating.  T=
he same branch design concept when used in larger diameters do not deliver =
standard passing performance regardless of the size of the boss.

The 6" and 8" Tapped Tee's employ an internal reinforcement and extended br=
anches.  See the fourth and fifth attachments.  This arrangement allows the=
se fittings to pass the testing requirements of AWWA C907 to warrant a pres=
sure rating.  The branches of these sizes maintain constant thickness relat=
ive to the female thread diameter unlike the 4" branch and use a thinner (b=
ut still thick) thickness because the branch is extended.  This permits enh=
anced control during the molding process.

j






